[CENTER][SIZE=6][B]MC Data Bridge[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][I]High-Performance, Secure, and Universal Player Data Synchronization[/I][/SIZE][/CENTER]

MC Data Bridge is a high-performance hybrid synchronization suite for [B]Paper/Spigot[/B], [B]Folia[/B], [B]BungeeCord[/B], and [B]Velocity[/B]. Designed for high-traffic production networks, it ensures a seamless cross-server experience by synchronizing health, hunger, experience, inventories, ender chests, advancements, recipes, vanilla statistics, companion pets, and PDC metadata with zero lag and industrial-grade security.

[SIZE=5]► Quick Start[/SIZE]

[LIST=1]
[*][B]Deploy Plugin:[/B] Place the single [I]mc-data-bridge-*.jar[/I] file into the [I]plugins/[/I] folder of each Minecraft server (Paper/Folia/Spigot) and your proxy (Velocity/Bungee).
[*][B]Configure Backend:[/B] Edit [I]plugins/mc-data-bridge/config.yml[/I] on each backend server. Set a unique [I]server-id[/I] (e.g., "survival-1"), enter MySQL/MariaDB credentials, and set [I]security.seed[/I] to a secret random string.
[*][B]Restart & Sync:[/B] Restart all components. Data synchronization runs automatically.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5]► Key Features[/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Universal Single-JAR Hybrid:[/B] A single JAR file operates across Spigot, Paper, Folia, BungeeCord, and Velocity, automatically activating the correct platform handlers.
[*][B]Comprehensive Cross-Server Sync:[/B] Synchronizes health, food level/saturation/exhaustion, experience, inventories, armor, potion effects, ender chests, advancements, recipes, vanilla statistics, PDC metadata, flight/gamemode states, companions/pets, maps, and separate gamemode profiles.
[*][B]Event-Driven Lock Release Messaging:[/B] Source servers dispatch an instant [I]LockReleased[/I] signal upon saving player state, waking destination pre-login threads immediately and reducing server-switch lock wait latency to ~50ms.
[*][B]Distributed Lock Fencing Tokens ([I]lock_version[/I]):[/B] Employs monotonic generation counters to fence off stale server writes, ensuring delayed servers (e.g. post-GC pauses) can never overwrite active player sessions.
[*][B]Single-Transaction Atomic Persistence:[/B] Combines normalized component updates ([I]databridge_inventories[/I], [I]statistics[/I], [I]metadata[/I], [I]companions[/I], [I]maps[/I]) and lock releases into a single database transaction ([I]setAutoCommit(false)[/I] ... [I]commit()[/I]).
[*][B]Keyed HMAC-SHA256 & Data Integrity Checksums:[/B] Standard [I]HmacSHA256[/I] key derivation with server salting protects player identities and detects database tampering across normalized component tables.
[*][B]Identity Modes & Auto-Migration:[/B] Supports [I]PREMIUM[/I] or [I]HYBRID[/I] identity modes. Integrates with FastLogin (PreLogin) and AuthMe (Login, 2FA/TOTP) for automatic offline-to-online UUID data migration.
[*][B]Interactive Inventory & Ender Chest Inspector ([I]invsee[/I] / [I]endersee[/I]):[/B] Inspect or interactively edit offline/cross-server player inventories in real time ([I]--edit[/I] flag or Right-Click) with automatic database persistence upon GUI close.
[*][B]Regionalized Folia Support:[/B] Fully compatible with Folia's regionalized threading model, ensuring safe data handling on modern multi-threaded server clusters.
[*][B]Embedded Prometheus Exporter:[/B] HTTP [I]/metrics[/I] endpoint to monitor HikariCP connection pools, transaction latencies, active queries, and cache efficiency.
[*][B]Granular Sync & Blacklist Control:[/B] Per-component toggles and server/world blacklists in [I]config.yml[/I].
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5]► Commands & Permissions[/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]/databridge inspect <player> [inventory|enderchest] [--edit][/B]
[LIST]
[*]Opens GUI to view or edit saved player data/inventory.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.inspect[/I] / [I]databridge.inspect.edit[/I] (for [I]--edit[/I])
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge invsee <player> [--edit][/B]
[LIST]
[*]Opens saved player inventory view or edit GUI.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.inspect[/I] / [I]databridge.inspect.edit[/I] (for [I]--edit[/I])
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge endersee <player> [--edit][/B]
[LIST]
[*]Opens saved player ender chest view or edit GUI.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.inspect[/I] / [I]databridge.inspect.edit[/I] (for [I]--edit[/I])
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge migrate <src> <dest>[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Securely move data between two identities.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.admin[/I]
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge unlock <player>[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Manually release a stuck data lock (works on Spigot, Folia, Bungee, Velocity).
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.admin[/I]
[/LIST]
[*][B]/databridge reload[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Reloads the configuration and DB pool.
[*]Permission: [I]databridge.admin[/I]
[/LIST]
[/LIST]

[B]Proxy Commands:[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]/databridge unlock <player>[/B] (Bungee/Velocity): Releases a lock across the network.
[*][B]/databridge forceunlock <player>[/B] (Bungee/Velocity): Relays a signal to the backend server to drop the lock immediately.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]Permission Nodes:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]databridge.inspect[/B]: Permission to view player data, inventories, and ender chests in safe read-only mode.
[*][B]databridge.inspect.edit[/B]: Elevated permission required to interactively edit inventories and ender chests via [I]--edit[/I] or Right-Click.
[*][B]databridge.admin[/B]: Master administrative access for all commands and functions.
[/LIST]

